    {
      "id": "541",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 541,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "さ and み both nominalize adjectives, similar to '~ness' in English, but differ in nuance and usage. さ works with both い and な-adjectives and expresses measurable degree, e.g. 高さ 'height' or 大変さ 'difficulty'. み is typically used with い-adjectives and focuses on quality or characteristics rather than degree, e.g. 面白み 'that which makes (something) interesting'.",
        "first_relatable": {
